{"input_text": "Question: I have a code in Matlab, and in one step it calculates Gamma function for different values. But when I try to find Gamma(172.5)  I get inf as it is bigger than realmax. My question:  is there a away that I can get and calculate  big numbera like Gamma (172.5) in Matlab without getting inf? 
 Thanks 

Answer: Yes, you can if you have the Symbolic toolbox. Then you can work with the variable-precision arithmetic. E.g.,  gamma(vpa(172.5))  or  vpa(gamma(sym(172.5)))  or 
 syms x real; 
y = subs(gamma(x),x,172.5); 
